>  - fail to read a spellbook of fire, effect same as a fire trap
>  - fail to read a spellbook of polymorph, affected as if poly trap
>  - fail to read charm monster, a nearby pet gets untamed
>  - fail to read detect monsters, monsters on level detect you &
> aggravate
>  - fail to read magic mapping, un-maps the current level
>  - fail to read identify, partial amnesia (for objects only)
>  ... etc. ...

Well, I don't think just reading a book should cause a magical effect.
It would, however, be nice if such effects were put in place when you
unsuccessfully *cast* a spell. Then, you would really have to be careful
to cast spells you hardly have any chance of succeeding at.

I wouldn't advocate a flat-out negative effect, in this case, just a
percentage chance that, *when* you fail to successfully cast a spell, it
will backfire.

This should be a rare occurrance: just a 5% chance *when* you fail your
casting should be enough.

